{
  "answer": "Large language models are memory-bound because they must repeatedly read massive parameter matrices from high-bandwidth memory for every single token generated. Since the computational units (GPUs) are often idle waiting for this data to arrive, the speed of data transfer becomes the primary bottleneck rather than raw processing power. Consequently, increasing memory bandwidth allows the GPU to fetch parameters faster, directly reducing the latency between generating one token and the next.",
